      "content": "but it feels way too specific for just \"subtle cues.\" the red cloud for the crash, then later i saw this intense violet shimmer right before a piece of equipment in the lab spontaneously shorted out. it feels like i'm seeing the mathematical weight of an event before it carries out. if my neurons were actually integrated with these particles, wouldn't that effectively turn my visual cortex into a biological sensor for probability densities? like, if we assume the particle stream had a quantum entanglement component, could my brain be perceiving the collapse of the wave function in real-time?",
